{ And finally as a small bonus, I will show a tiny portion of an opening I have named and analyzed, the Rudramandov Grand Prix. It starts with the usual moves. }
1. e4 c5 2. Nc3 Nc6 { Here, what you should do is try to get rid of this bishop, by developing it to b5 } { [%csl Rc6][%cal Gf1b5] } 3. Bb5 { This is the Rudramandov. It is like the Rossolimo but your f- pawn is not blocked by your knight. Here the opponent has several options which I will cover in my next study. } *

